+# Broadcom research record
+
+Accessed 2026-08-15. These are the pages actually fetched while producing the architecture.
+
+- **Update Sequence for VCF 9.0 and Compatible VMware Products**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/390634/update-sequence-for-vcf-90-and-compatibl.html
+  Informed the management-component order, the Aria Suite Lifecycle 8.18 Patch 2 prerequisite, Operations 8.14+ eligibility, and the fresh Logs deployment with a maximum 90-day data transfer.
+
+- **Upgrading Aria Operations 8.x to newer version failed with error “Failed The PAK action”**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/382152/upgrading-aria-operations-8x-to-newer-ve.html
+  Informed the mandatory 8.17.2 intermediate hop for an Operations 8.10.2 source before a later upgrade.
+
+- **How to re-trigger VCF Automation 9.0 failed upgrade workflow**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/398777/how-to-retrigger-vcf-automation-90-faile.html
+  Confirmed that an existing Aria Automation 8.18 deployment is imported into Fleet Management before its managed 9.0 upgrade.
+
+- **After upgrading Aria Automation 8.18 to VCF Automation 9.0, the login URL changed**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/422762/after-upgrading-aria-automation-818-to-v.html
+  Informed abandonment of legacy CSP bookmarks and the VCF Identity Broker login cutover.
+
+- **Users unable to view existing deployments after upgrading from Aria Automation 8.18 to VCF Automation 9.0.x**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/434594/users-unable-to-view-their-existing-depl.html
+  Informed the identity-case review gate and post-upgrade deployment-ownership remediation.
+
+- **Upgrade Guidance for Aria Operations for Logs 8.18.x to VCF Operations for Logs 9.0.x**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/402314
+  Confirmed that no in-place Logs upgrade exists, that parallel operation is supported, and that integrations are reconfigured on the fresh target.
+
+- **Aria Operations for Logs Data Transfer Fails Immediately with “Transfer failed due to an error”**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/437089/aria-operations-for-logs-data-transfer-f.html
+  Informed the vCenter-license, TCP 7000/7001, and time-synchronization gates for historical-data transfer.
+
+- **End of General Support for VMware Aria Operations 8.18**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/422643/end-of-general-support-for-vmware-aria-o.html
+  Confirmed the 2027-10-11 support boundary for the 8.18 Operations generation and the move to VCF Operations 9.0.
+
+- **Build numbers and versions for VMware Aria Automation**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/318130/build-numbers-and-versions-for-vmware-ar.html
+  Confirmed the Aria Automation 8.18.1 release identity and its 2027-10-11 end-of-general-support boundary.
+
+- **Broadcom announces EOGS for Aria Operations Management Pack for Horizon**
+  https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/392309/broadcom-is-announcing-end-of-general-su.html
+  Informed the decision to abandon the inventoried Horizon 2.7 management pack rather than carry it into the accepted target.
+
+- **VCF Virtual Networking Technical Reference – VCF 9.0**
+  https://community.broadcom.com/applications-networking-security/viewdocument/vcf-virtual-networking-technical-re
+  Informed the dedicated Edge-cluster, dual-leaf, multiple-uplink layout used to realize the pinned throughput sizing.
